### Directions for how to execute Scrubbing on your p3k14c dataset before analysis:

# Clone the official scrubbing repository
!git clone https://github.com/people3k/p3k14c-data-scrubbing.git

# Change the working directory to the cloned repo
%cd p3k14c-data-scrubbing

# Install the required dependencies listed in their documentation
!pip install numpy pandas ftfy tqdm pyshp shapely matplotlib pyproj

# Define your file paths
raw_data = "../p3k14c_raw.csv"     # Your raw, uncleaned CSV
scrubbed_data = "scrubbed.csv"     # The output cleaned CSV
graveyard = "graveyard.csv"        # A log of everything deleted and WHY

# Run the main scrubber via the command line
!python scrub.py {raw_data} {scrubbed_data} {graveyard}

# Define the final output name
final_ready_data = "p3k14c_final_ready.csv"

# Run the fuzzing script on the scrubbed data
!python fuzz/fuzz.py {scrubbed_data} {final_ready_data}

# Generates a table of suggested substitutions based on the GeoNames dataset
!python charfix/correct.py {final_ready_data} suggested_fixes.csv

# Once you review suggested_fixes.csv, you can apply them
!python charfix/applyFixes.py {final_ready_data} suggested_fixes.csv final_fixed_names.csv

